			"notes": "Seed Atlas works again on Forge and NeoForge.\n\n## Fixed\n- On Forge and NeoForge, Seed Atlas switched itself off on every start with \"Disabled: the installed Xaero's World Map changed something this Seed Atlas version relies on (Missing Xaero class xaero/map/gui/GuiMap (+11 more))\", whichever Xaero's World Map version was installed. Xaero had not changed anything: the loaders' Mixin services refuse to hand out untransformed classes, and Seed Atlas mistook that for missing Xaero classes. It now reads the classes straight from the mod jars.\n- If a class ever cannot be read, the log now says so instead of blaming a Xaero update.\n\nFabric was not affected.\n\n## Downloads\nPick the jar for your Minecraft version and loader:\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | Forge | NeoForge |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 26.1.2 | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.1.2-fabric.jar` | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.1.2-forge.jar` | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.1.2-neoforge.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.2-fabric.jar` | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.2-forge.jar` | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.2-neoforge.jar` |\n| 26.3 | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.3-fabric.jar` | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.3-forge.jar` | `seedatlas-xaero-2.0.1-mc26.3-neoforge.jar` |\n\nRequires Xaero's World Map 1.47.1 or newer. SHA-256 checksums are in `SHA256SUMS.txt`."
		},
